{"authored" [{"question" "q-96833" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the standard Hermitian inner product $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ over $C.$ \nWhich of the following statements are true? \n\n- $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$\n- $⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C$\n- $⟨a,b⟩\\in R$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7161402bb26a8d3d1c103f3056e10281c142b7cef56025b01cb00441814a8a4" "basis" 1447 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-96833" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the standard Hermitian inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties:\n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, the inner product over $C$ has conjugate symmetry.\n\n- Statement II is false. To factor out a constant multiple from the second argument, we must change it to its complex conjugate.\n\n- Statement III is false. The inner product over $C$ is a complex number in general.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7161402bb26a8d3d1c103f3056e10281c142b7cef56025b01cb00441814a8a4" "basis" 1447 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-96833" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b9aea95bc2b0f3d0948763302c4c26ff7579af434895f23f3da082a34876c014" "basis" 1447 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-96833" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7161402bb26a8d3d1c103f3056e10281c142b7cef56025b01cb00441814a8a4" "basis" 1447 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-96833" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7161402bb26a8d3d1c103f3056e10281c142b7cef56025b01cb00441814a8a4" "basis" 1447 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-96833" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7161402bb26a8d3d1c103f3056e10281c142b7cef56025b01cb00441814a8a4" "basis" 1447 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-96833" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7161402bb26a8d3d1c103f3056e10281c142b7cef56025b01cb00441814a8a4" "basis" 1447 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-96833" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7161402bb26a8d3d1c103f3056e10281c142b7cef56025b01cb00441814a8a4" "basis" 1447 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-96833" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7161402bb26a8d3d1c103f3056e10281c142b7cef56025b01cb00441814a8a4" "basis" 1447 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97258" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the standard Hermitian inner product $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ over $C.$ \nWhich of the following statements are true? \n\n- $⟨a,a⟩\\in R$ for any $a\\in {C}^{n}$\n- $⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C$\n- $⟨a,b⟩=⟨b,a⟩$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7161402bb26a8d3d1c103f3056e10281c142b7cef56025b01cb00441814a8a4" "basis" 1447 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97258" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the standard Hermitian inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties:\n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements. \n\n- Statement I is true. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$  $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number.\n\n- Statement II is false. To factor out a constant multiple from the second argument, we must change it to its complex conjugate.\n\n- Statement III is false. The inner product over $C$ has conjugate symmetry.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7161402bb26a8d3d1c103f3056e10281c142b7cef56025b01cb00441814a8a4" "basis" 1447 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97258" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b9aea95bc2b0f3d0948763302c4c26ff7579af434895f23f3da082a34876c014" "basis" 1447 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97258" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7161402bb26a8d3d1c103f3056e10281c142b7cef56025b01cb00441814a8a4" "basis" 1447 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97258" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7161402bb26a8d3d1c103f3056e10281c142b7cef56025b01cb00441814a8a4" "basis" 1447 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97258" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7161402bb26a8d3d1c103f3056e10281c142b7cef56025b01cb00441814a8a4" "basis" 1447 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97258" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "II and III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7161402bb26a8d3d1c103f3056e10281c142b7cef56025b01cb00441814a8a4" "basis" 1447 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97258" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7161402bb26a8d3d1c103f3056e10281c142b7cef56025b01cb00441814a8a4" "basis" 1447 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97258" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7161402bb26a8d3d1c103f3056e10281c142b7cef56025b01cb00441814a8a4" "basis" 1447 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97258" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7161402bb26a8d3d1c103f3056e10281c142b7cef56025b01cb00441814a8a4" "basis" 1447 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97159" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ is the standard Hermitian inner product over $C,$ find $⟨a,\\,6b+c⟩$ if   \n\n$\\,$ $⟨b,a⟩=2+3\\text{i}\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,c⟩=3+8\\text{i}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7161402bb26a8d3d1c103f3056e10281c142b7cef56025b01cb00441814a8a4" "basis" 1447 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97159" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties. \n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nFirst, we use the fact that the inner product over $C$ is antilinear in the second argument:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨a,\\,6b+c⟩ & =⟨a,6b⟩+⟨a,c⟩ \\\\  & =\\overset{―}{6}⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩ \\\\  & =6⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nNext, we use the fact that the inner product over $C$ has conjugate symmetry: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩ & =6\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}+⟨a,c⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute the values for $⟨b,a⟩$ and $⟨a,c⟩:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}+⟨a,c⟩ & =6(\\overset{―}{2+3\\text{i}})+(3+8\\text{i}) \\\\  & =6(2-3\\text{i})+(3+8\\text{i}) \\\\  & =12-18\\text{i}+3+8\\text{i} \\\\  & =15-10\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7161402bb26a8d3d1c103f3056e10281c142b7cef56025b01cb00441814a8a4" "basis" 1447 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97159" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b9aea95bc2b0f3d0948763302c4c26ff7579af434895f23f3da082a34876c014" "basis" 1447 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97159" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7161402bb26a8d3d1c103f3056e10281c142b7cef56025b01cb00441814a8a4" "basis" 1447 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97159" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1+8\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7161402bb26a8d3d1c103f3056e10281c142b7cef56025b01cb00441814a8a4" "basis" 1447 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97159" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-5+7\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7161402bb26a8d3d1c103f3056e10281c142b7cef56025b01cb00441814a8a4" "basis" 1447 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97159" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "15-10\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7161402bb26a8d3d1c103f3056e10281c142b7cef56025b01cb00441814a8a4" "basis" 1447 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97159" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "3-5\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7161402bb26a8d3d1c103f3056e10281c142b7cef56025b01cb00441814a8a4" "basis" 1447 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97159" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "7-\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7161402bb26a8d3d1c103f3056e10281c142b7cef56025b01cb00441814a8a4" "basis" 1447 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97159" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "15-10\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7161402bb26a8d3d1c103f3056e10281c142b7cef56025b01cb00441814a8a4" "basis" 1447 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97215" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ is the standard Hermitian inner product over $C,$ find $⟨6a+4b,\\,c⟩$ if \n\n$\\,$ $⟨c,a⟩=2+4\\text{i}\\,$ and $\\,⟨c,b⟩=-5-3\\text{i}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7161402bb26a8d3d1c103f3056e10281c142b7cef56025b01cb00441814a8a4" "basis" 1447 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97215" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties. \n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nFirst, we use the fact that the inner product over $C$ is linear in the first argument: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨6a+4b,\\,c⟩ & =⟨6a,c⟩+⟨4b,c⟩ \\\\  & =6⟨a,c⟩+4⟨b,c⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we use the fact that the inner product over $C$ has conjugate symmetry: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6⟨a,c⟩+4⟨b,c⟩ & =6\\overset{―}{⟨c,a⟩}+4\\overset{―}{⟨c,b⟩}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute the values for $⟨c,a⟩$ and $⟨c,b⟩:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6\\overset{―}{⟨c,a⟩}+4\\overset{―}{⟨c,b⟩} & =6(\\overset{―}{2+4\\text{i}})+4\\overset{―}{(-5-3\\text{i})} \\\\  & =6(2-4\\text{i})+4(-5+3\\text{i}) \\\\  & =12-24\\text{i}-20+12\\text{i} \\\\  & =-8-12\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7161402bb26a8d3d1c103f3056e10281c142b7cef56025b01cb00441814a8a4" "basis" 1447 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97215" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b9aea95bc2b0f3d0948763302c4c26ff7579af434895f23f3da082a34876c014" "basis" 1447 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97215" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7161402bb26a8d3d1c103f3056e10281c142b7cef56025b01cb00441814a8a4" "basis" 1447 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97215" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3+\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7161402bb26a8d3d1c103f3056e10281c142b7cef56025b01cb00441814a8a4" "basis" 1447 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97215" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-8-12\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7161402bb26a8d3d1c103f3056e10281c142b7cef56025b01cb00441814a8a4" "basis" 1447 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97215" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "12+8\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7161402bb26a8d3d1c103f3056e10281c142b7cef56025b01cb00441814a8a4" "basis" 1447 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97215" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "3-\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7161402bb26a8d3d1c103f3056e10281c142b7cef56025b01cb00441814a8a4" "basis" 1447 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97215" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "8+12\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7161402bb26a8d3d1c103f3056e10281c142b7cef56025b01cb00441814a8a4" "basis" 1447 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97215" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-8-12\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7161402bb26a8d3d1c103f3056e10281c142b7cef56025b01cb00441814a8a4" "basis" 1447 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040565/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-141159" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the standard Hermitian inner product $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ over $C.$ \nWhich of the following statements are true? \n\n- $⟨a,b⟩=⟨b,a⟩$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$\n- $⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in R$\n- $⟨a,a⟩>0$ for any $a\\in {C}^{n}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071006/state.json" "file_sha256" "382c640f7299b58b35ff8d7f8d04188375abf6d077b621043508735c29fe710b" "basis" 2542 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071006/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-141159" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the standard Hermitian inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties:\n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. The inner product over $C$ has conjugate symmetry.\n\n- Statement II is true. For any $\\alpha \\in R,$ we have $\\overset{―}{\\alpha }=\\alpha .$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Notice that if $a=0,$ then $⟨a,a⟩=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071006/state.json" "file_sha256" "382c640f7299b58b35ff8d7f8d04188375abf6d077b621043508735c29fe710b" "basis" 2542 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071006/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-141159" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071006/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6c85a7049ebf13f24aced7e0921c06a01dd7d94d8f90ecfa05f88253d382e440" "basis" 2542 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071006/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-141159" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071006/state.json" "file_sha256" "382c640f7299b58b35ff8d7f8d04188375abf6d077b621043508735c29fe710b" "basis" 2542 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071006/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-141159" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071006/state.json" "file_sha256" "382c640f7299b58b35ff8d7f8d04188375abf6d077b621043508735c29fe710b" "basis" 2542 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071006/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-141159" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071006/state.json" "file_sha256" "382c640f7299b58b35ff8d7f8d04188375abf6d077b621043508735c29fe710b" "basis" 2542 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071006/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-141159" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071006/state.json" "file_sha256" "382c640f7299b58b35ff8d7f8d04188375abf6d077b621043508735c29fe710b" "basis" 2542 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071006/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-141159" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071006/state.json" "file_sha256" "382c640f7299b58b35ff8d7f8d04188375abf6d077b621043508735c29fe710b" "basis" 2542 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071006/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-141159" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071006/state.json" "file_sha256" "382c640f7299b58b35ff8d7f8d04188375abf6d077b621043508735c29fe710b" "basis" 2542 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071006/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-96833" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the standard Hermitian inner product $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ over $C.$ \nWhich of the following statements are true? \n\n- $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$\n- $⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C$\n- $⟨a,b⟩\\in R$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072618/state.json" "file_sha256" "d545f26c58882e94a7d39026a6875a82f64222304cf6e504e04bc4d9273f850e"} {"question" "q-96833" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the standard Hermitian inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties:\n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, the inner product over $C$ has conjugate symmetry.\n\n- Statement II is false. To factor out a constant multiple from the second argument, we must change it to its complex conjugate.\n\n- Statement III is false. The inner product over $C$ is a complex number in general.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072618/state.json" "file_sha256" "d545f26c58882e94a7d39026a6875a82f64222304cf6e504e04bc4d9273f850e"} {"question" "q-96833" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072618/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cbf5fa7da243b5d2aef61d6766bc47fcfbad8ad51341d80e7e3e2bdeb26f7fe0"} {"question" "q-96833" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "